To sort an array of items by their id and then count together the ids, you can use the following TypeScript function:

```typescript
interface Item {
  id: number;
}

function sortAndSumIds(items: Item[]): number {
  const sortedItems = items.sort((a, b) => a.id - b.id);
  return sortedItems.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.id, 0);
}
```

This function first sorts the array of items by their id using the `sort` method. It then uses the `reduce` method to sum up the ids of the sorted items. The result is the sum of the ids after sorting.
